        "content": "## New Client Radar, companies that just started hiring\n\nA company posting new roles is a company with fresh budget and an urgent problem. This watches your niche every morning for businesses that posted jobs in the last 24 hours, groups the postings by company so one growing team is one lead rather than five noisy job ads, drafts a two line outreach opener for each, and files everything in a Google Sheet.\n\n### Setup, about 5 minutes\n\n1. **Apify account.** Free account at apify.com, then Settings, then API & Integrations. Copy your Personal API token. Open *Fetch Fresh Job Postings* and create an Apify API credential with it. On n8n Cloud you can pick OAuth2 instead and just sign in. If the Apify node is missing, install the verified community node `@apify/n8n-nodes-apify` from the nodes panel.\n2. **Radar Settings.** Describe your niche: the roles that signal a good client, the industries, company sizes and locations you serve, and what you offer.\n3. **Connect OpenAI, Google Sheets and Slack**, then pick your channel and spreadsheet.\n4. **Google Sheet.** Header row: Date Found, Company, Industry, Company Size, Open Roles, Role Titles, Locations, Website, AI Opener, Job Links\n5. Activate the workflow.\n\n### Good to know\n\n- Only direct employers are returned. Staffing and recruiting agencies are filtered out at the source, so you never pitch a competitor.\n- Companies you have already been shown are remembered between runs, so the same lead never appears twice.\n- On quiet days nothing is sent.\n- The Hirebase jobs feed on Apify is pay per result at $3 per 1,000 jobs, billed to your own Apify account."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "fa0affcd-41ed-40df-b28f-74066bc6da74",
      "name": "Sticky Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        336,
        176
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 450,
        "height": 470,
        "content": "## 1. Describe your niche here\n\nOpen **Radar Settings**. The next node turns your answers into a valid API request, so you never edit JSON.\n\n- **jobTitles / keywords**: comma separated, at least one required\n- **industries**: separate with semicolons, because some industry names contain a comma. Example: Tech, Software & IT Services; Healthcare\n- **companySizes**: 1-10, 11-50, 51-200, 201-500, 501-1000, 1001-5000, 5001-10000, 10000+\n- **locations**: separate with semicolons\n- **locationTypes**: Remote, Hybrid, In-Person\n- **whatYouOffer**: finishes the sentence \"openers are written on behalf of ...\"\n- **minOpenRoles**: ignore companies with fewer new roles than this\n- **hotLeadRoles**: this many roles or more gets an instant alert"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "be027835-2609-4cf8-9233-03462bbe1fc0",
      "name": "Sticky Note 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1520,
        224
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 460,
        "content": "## 2. Turning job ads into one lead\n\n**Group Postings by Company** is the heart of this workflow. Five job ads from one company are not five leads, they are one strong signal. This collapses them into a single record with the role count, the role titles and the locations.\n\n**Skip Companies Already Pitched** remembers every company from previous runs, so you never see, or pitch, the same company twice.\n\n**Enough Open Roles to Count** drops weak signals before the AI step, so you spend nothing generating copy for a company that posted one junior role.\n\nIf the job feed is unreachable, the error branch posts a failure notice to Slack instead of failing silently."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "4ef1133a-d47d-419b-be23-cf0d561a1ad7",
      "name": "Sticky Note 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2400,
        208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 380,
        "content": "## 3. Where leads go\n\n**Hot lead**, meaning at least your hot lead threshold of roles: an instant Slack alert with the drafted opener, so you can reach out while the need is fresh.\n\n**Standard lead**: batched into one morning digest posted to Slack.\n\nEvery lead, hot or standard, is appended to your Google Sheet with its opener, so the sheet becomes your prospecting pipeline. Swap this node for your CRM if you prefer."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
